# Construction placement feedback and plan preview

Make ghost placement visible before returning to the editor and provide a read-only preview of the plan's projected board.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] After a valid planned construction is placed, its ghost remains visible on the placement Board for 0.65 seconds.
- [x] The placement screen returns to the construction editor only after that delay.
- [x] Invalid placement remains on screen and continues to use REQ-012's two-second error feedback.
- [x] The construction editor has a button whose icon resembles a group of hexagons.
- [x] Tapping the preview button opens the Board with all current plan steps rendered as ghost pieces.
- [x] Preview mode does not expose placement targets and cannot mutate the real Board or plan.
- [x] Preview has an obvious Close/Back action that returns to the same editor draft.
- [x] Real and ghost roads render behind real and ghost settlements/cities.
- [x] App and test bundles compile with relevant timing and navigation coverage.
- [ ] Focused UI checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- Depends on TASK-012's ordered construction steps, projected Board state, and ghost renderer.
- Keep the 0.65-second delay cancellable so dismissing the placement screen cannot append twice or navigate later unexpectedly.

## Verification

- Add deterministic state/timing coverage where possible and manual checks for ghost visibility and preview readability.

## Evidence

- Valid placement immediately renders the selected ghost and confirmation, disables further targets, and uses a cancellable 650 ms task before appending once and dismissing.
- Board rendering uses explicit road layers before building layers, including separate ghost-road and ghost-building passes.
- Added a hex-cluster preview button and a read-only full-screen Board preview with the draft's projected ghost pieces and an accessible Close action.
- Extended UI coverage for the visible delay, preview navigation, absent placement targets, and return to the unchanged editor draft.
